{{!
    Shared footer for every Friends with Habits view. Registered as a Handlebars
    partial in server-client.tsx, so views include it by the partial name
    habitsFooter.

    Keep the markup here rather than copied per view: the footers drifted apart
    once already (three different link sets and two different copyright lines
    across nine templates), and this is the surface search crawlers use to walk
    between the two properties.

    Two things this comment must not contain, both of which broke the footer on
    every habits page when they were in here:

      1. A partial call. Handlebars does not treat an HTML comment as a comment,
         so naming this block's own partial inside one still executes it, and the
         footer recursed into itself until the stack blew.
      2. A Handlebars comment delimiter. The long comment form ends at the FIRST
         closing delimiter, even one written inside backticks as prose, so the
         rest of the block leaked onto the rendered page as visible text. Hence
         the short bare-bang form here.

    The styles it depends on - footer.site-footer, .footer-links, .footer-family
    and .container - live in each view's own style block, since these templates
    are otherwise self-contained and have no shared stylesheet.
}}
<footer class="site-footer">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="footer-links">
            <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>
            <a href="/terms-of-service">Terms of Service</a>
            <a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.therr.habits" rel="noopener">Google Play</a>
        </div>
        <div>&copy; Therr Inc.</div>
        <!--
            Outbound link to the sibling property. habits.therr.com is a brand-new
            subdomain with no inbound links of its own; the reciprocal link in the
            therr.app footer is what gives crawlers a path to it from an indexed
            domain, and this side ties the two entities together.
        -->
        <div class="footer-family">
            Part of the Therr family of apps &mdash;
            <a href="https://www.therr.app/" rel="noopener">Therr, for local discovery and community</a>.
        </div>
    </div>
</footer>
